From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] A screen being held is not an application to wait for

With 0071 the hold works: on the device (2026-11-03,
eng.builde.20261103.032804), with the deadline shortened to 2 s and the starting
window off, the outgoing launcher reads isOnScreen=true at 4 s, 9 s and 25 s
where the same run with the hold turned off reads false at 4 s and shows the
status bar and the navigation bar over black. The reader sees the launcher until
WeRead's shelf arrives, and never a blank screen.

What does not work is letting go. No "letting go" line was logged, and 25 s in,
with the shelf on the screen, a dump showed both sets still full:

    mHeldOverClosingApps={...weread.LauncherActivity, ...launcher3/.Launcher}
    mHeldOverOpeningApps={...weread.LauncherActivity, ...WeReadFragmentActivity}

WeRead's launcher activity is in both. It is a trampoline: it opens in the first
transition and is the screen being held in the second, and it finishes without
ever drawing. 0069 asked for the release "when every application that was
opening has something on screen", which that one makes false for good; and
"when all of them have gone away" is false too, because the hold is what is
keeping it. The two conditions can never both be reached, so the hold stayed,
the launcher's surface stayed, and the activity manager and the window manager
disagreed about it until the next transition.

Three changes, which are one idea said three times: what is being held is not
what is being waited for.

  * A token added to the held screens is removed from the ones waited for.
  * The release asks that none of them is *still coming*, rather than that all
    of them have drawn: each is either on the screen, or gone, or not yet, and
    only the last of those holds the release back.
  * A held screen that has gone away is skipped rather than hidden; there is
    nothing there to hide, and setVisibility() on it reaches into a container
    the window manager has already let go of.

The states this separates, written out because the previous three attempts each
died on a case that was not: an application that has not drawn yet, one that has
gone away, one that became the screen being held, and one that drew. Before
this, the second and third read the same as the first.

Not run on the device yet when this patch was written.

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowSurfacePlacer.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowSurfacePlacer.java
@@ -489,6 +489,15 @@
